[; Validate a config document by asking the SHAPE questions rather than
   walking it: does a port exist, does a host exist. The document is data and
   the check is a path query over it, which is the whole point of the exercise.
   Rewritten for the v0.8.0 surface (RULED: VC-28); the original was
   pre-reshape (`[?let $x = … :in]`, `count(…)` call-parens, `:backoff 100ms`
   atom-as-attribute-name). ]
[?let [= $config [config
                   [port 8080]
                   [host "localhost"]
                   [retry max=3 backoff=100ms]]]
  [?match true
    [when [$and [> [$count $config//port] 0] [> [$count $config//host] 0]] :valid]
    [else :invalid]]]
